{"content":[{"c":["ELIHU"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Ephraimite, Tohu’s son and an ancestor of Samuel the prophet (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.1","r":"1Sam.1.1","rawR":"1Sam.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.1","value":"1Sam.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:1"},"); perhaps also called Eliab and Eliel in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.27,34","r":"1Chr.6.27,34","rawR":"1Chr.6.27,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.27,34","value":"1Chr.6.27,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:27, 34"},", respectively."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. One of the soldiers of Manasseh’s tribe who joined up with David’s army at Ziklag (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.20","r":"1Chr.12.20","rawR":"1Chr.12.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.20","value":"1Chr.12.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 12:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Korahite Levite and a gatekeeper of the tabernacle during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.7","r":"1Chr.26.7","rawR":"1Chr.26.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.7","value":"1Chr.26.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Alternate name for Eliab, David’s eldest brother, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.18","r":"1Chr.27.18","rawR":"1Chr.27.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.18","value":"1Chr.27.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 27:18"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Eliab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Eliab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Eliab_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Eliab #3"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. One of Job’s friends, a Buzite, the son of Barachel (",{"href":"?bref=Job.32.2","r":"Job.32.2","rawR":"Job.32.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.32.2","value":"Job.32.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 32:2"},"). He spoke about suffering as a form of discipline after three of Job’s friends failed to answer Job’s arguments (chs ",{"href":"?bref=Job.32.1-37.24","r":"Job.32.1-37.24","rawR":"Job.32.1-37.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.32.1-37.24","value":"Job.32.1-37.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"32–37"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elihu","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.1.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 6:27, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.27,34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.27,34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.27,34"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 12:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.12.20","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.12.20","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.12.20"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 27:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.18"},{"anchorText":"Jb 32:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.32.2","rawQueryValue":"Job.32.2","sourceRefExact":"Job.32.2"},{"anchorText":"32–37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.32.1-37.24","rawQueryValue":"Job.32.1-37.24","sourceRefExact":"Job.32.1-37.24"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3ddfdbe4e6cc8fb5db6dc01a03a900d9bf6f309808e16f2f7a9a484662685f54","sourceItemName":"Elihu","sourceItemOrder":101,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elihu","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elihu","title":"Elihu","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}